-- Arcana's Khonsu helpers, all in one file (ARC-0005, 2026-10-12): one disk open while the Toolkit loads the AI,
-- instead of one per function. Each section is one function; the names are what Stats conditions call.
-- IsWeaveSurge is generated by gen_emotion_alchemy.pl (55/_wip/Resonant/44_IsWeaveSurge.khn): update its section from there.

-- ===== IsCardSpell =====
-- "E uma carta" -- pela MARCA na condicao, nao pelo custo.
--
-- Antes isto era HasUseCosts('ArcanaHandCard'). Funcionava, mas o custo extra no UseCosts impedia o
-- motor de colapsar a carta base na variante de upcast do nivel que o personagem tem: base e variante
-- ficavam as duas no grimario e o jogo mostrava a caixa de Superconjurar. O Warlock, cujas magias
-- nao carregam nenhum custo alem do espaco, fica so com a variante -- e por isso nunca mostra caixa.
-- Confirmado em 2026-09-24 tirando o custo de uma carta de teste: a base sumiu, a caixa junto.
--
-- A marca e uma condicao sempre verdadeira, porque a passiva ARCANA_IS_CARD nao existe e nao deve
-- existir nunca. Pergunta pelo context.Source, que e sempre personagem, entao vale igual em magia de
-- alvo, de posicao e de area. E o padrao do jogo base: a Larian enfia 'SculptSpells' no
-- TargetConditions de 34 magias e as reconhece com HasStringInSpellConditions.
--
-- Carta nova precisa da marca no TargetConditions -- o gerador de variantes a propaga pelo `using`,
-- mas a entrada base e responsabilidade de quem a cria.
function IsCardSpell()
    return HasSpellFlag(SpellFlags.Spell) & HasStringInSpellConditions('ARCANA_IS_CARD')
end

-- ===== IsArcanaSpell =====
-- Any spell of the Arcana class: a card, or one of the class's own spells that is not a card (the
-- Distortion explosions, the clone's Sigil, the Gale Deflection ricochet, and the utilities aimed at
-- a creature or object: Friends, Dispel Magic, Dead Whispers, Arcane Lock/Unlock).
-- Cards carry ARCANA_IS_CARD in their TargetConditions (see IsCardSpell); the others carry
-- ARCANA_IS_SPELL, the same way. Reading a marker instead of listing names keeps every upcast
-- variant in: SpellId() compares the exact name, so a list missed the "..._3" of every card.
-- Used by the SIGIL mark (what detonates it) and by IsMirroredSelfSpell.
function IsArcanaSpell()
    return HasStringInSpellConditions('ARCANA_IS_CARD') | HasStringInSpellConditions('ARCANA_IS_SPELL')
end

-- ===== IsArcanaAttackSpell =====
function IsArcanaAttackSpell()
    return IsCardSpell() & HasStringInSpellRoll('Attack')
end
-- ===== IsArcanaCantrip =====
function IsArcanaCantrip()
    return SpellId('Target_Light')
    | SpellId('Shout_ProduceFlame')
    | SpellId('Shout_Arcana_Util_Faceless')
    | SpellId('Target_Arcana_Card_Spell_MaliciousWhispers')
    | SpellId('Shout_Arcana_Card_Spell_HowlOfTheDead')
    | SpellId('Target_TrueStrike')
    | SpellId('Target_Arcana_Util_DeadWhispers')
    | SpellId('Target_ChillTouch')
end

-- ===== IsArcanaSaveSpell =====
function IsArcanaSaveSpell()
    return IsCardSpell() & (HasStringInSpellRoll('SavingThrow') | HasStringInFunctorConditions('SavingThrow'))
end
-- ===== IsIsolatedFoe =====
-- Tier II do Aspecto de Death (ETERNAL_DREAD_AURA). No functor da aura, context.Source e o Eternal e
-- context.Target e o inimigo dentro dela. O inimigo esta isolado quando e o unico inimigo do Eternal a
-- ate 3 m e nenhum aliado dele esta a ate 6 m. Usa os mesmos construtores do HasEnemyWithinRange e do
-- HasAllyWithinRange do CommonConditions.khn do vanilla.
function IsIsolatedFoe()
    local foes = GetEnemiesWithinRange(3, context.Source, context.Source)
    local friends = GetAlliesWithinRange(6, context.Target, context.Target)
    local foeCount = 0
    if foes ~= nil then foeCount = #foes.Enemies end
    local friendCount = 0
    if friends ~= nil then friendCount = #friends.Allies end
    return ConditionResult(foeCount <= 1 and friendCount == 0)
end

-- ===== IsMirroredSelfSpell =====
-- What Mirrored Self twins: any Arcana spell aimed at creatures or objects, of any subclass.
-- Read from the spell's own properties, the way the base game's Twinned Spell does
-- (TwinnedTargetSpellCheck / TwinnedProjectileSpellCheck in CommonConditions.khn), so an upcast
-- variant, a new card or a marked utility counts without being listed anywhere. It replaced
-- IsDeceiverOneTargetSpell, a list of names: SpellId() compares the exact name, and the list lost
-- the icon glow on the cards that have upcast variants.
-- Unlike Twinned there is no "only one target" limit: a spell that gains targets by upcasting still
-- gets +1 (ModifyNumberOfTargets(AdditiveBase,...) adds, it does not override).
function IsMirroredSelfSpell()
    return IsArcanaSpell()
        & (SpellTypeIs(SpellType.Target) | SpellTypeIs(SpellType.Projectile))
        & ~AreaRadiusGreaterThan(0)
        & ~HasFunctor(StatsFunctorType.Summon)
end

-- ===== IsWeaveSurge =====
-- Any Weave Surge of the Resonant (ARC-0002, generated by gen_emotion_alchemy.pl -- do not edit by hand).
-- The 8 Surges carry ARCANA_IS_SURGE in their TargetConditions, an always-true marker (the passive does not exist);
-- reading the marker keeps every upcast variant in, which SpellId() would miss. Used by RESONANT_SURGE_FREE (Tier II).
function IsWeaveSurge()
    return HasStringInSpellConditions('ARCANA_IS_SURGE')
end

-- ===== UseSpellSlot =====
function UseSpellSlot()
    return HasSpellSpellLevel()
    & HasSpellFlag(SpellFlags.Spell)
    & (HasUseCosts('SpellSlotsGroup') | HasUseCosts('SpellSlot') | HasUseCosts('WarlockSpellSlot'))
end